<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kulikovo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1380</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kulikovo was fought on 8 September 1380 on Kulikovo Field near the upper Don, when an army of Russian principalities led by Grand Prince Dmitry of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> defeated the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamai">Mamai</a>, the warlord of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>. Although <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh">Tokhtamysh</a> sacked Moscow two years later, the victory earned Dmitry the name Donskoy and became a symbol of Russian resistance to Mongol rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kulikovo.jpg" alt="Battle of Kulikovo" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adolphe Yvon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dmitry_Donskoy_in_the_Battle_of_Kulikovo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
